Phase 1: Setup and authentication
Week 1. Working login with roles and an app shell.

Tasks
Create server and client (Vite) projects, init Git, add ESLint and Prettier
Create a MongoDB Atlas cluster, connect with Mongoose using .env
User model: name, email, passwordHash, role
Endpoints: POST /auth/register, POST /auth/login, GET /auth/me
bcrypt hashing and JWT signing
Middleware: auth, authorize(roles), errorHandler
React: Login page, AuthContext, ProtectedRoute, sidebar and navbar layout
Seed one admin user
Done when: A user can log in and see a role-based empty dashboard. Deploy this basic version early.

Phase 2: Inventory module
Weeks 2-3. Full product and stock management.

Tasks
Models: Category, Product (sku, prices, stockQty, reorderLevel), StockLog
CRUD APIs for categories and products with validation
Product list page with search, category filter and pagination
Add and edit product forms
POST /products/:id/adjust for manual stock changes, each writing a StockLog
stockService with a low-stock check
Low-stock list and navbar badge
Done when: Admins and managers can fully manage products and stock, and every change is logged.

Phase 3: Sales and purchase modules
Weeks 4-5. Orders that move stock automatically. The hardest phase.

Tasks
Customer and Supplier models with CRUD
SalesOrder: validate stock, then in one transaction save order, reduce stock, write StockLogs
PurchaseOrder: saved as ordered, then PATCH /purchases/:id/receive adds stock in a transaction
Status flows and cancellation rules that reverse stock correctly
Invoice number generation in invoiceService
Order forms with dynamic item rows, order lists, detail pages
Printable invoice page
Done when: Real sales and purchases keep stock correct, and cancelling an order restores it.

Phase 4: HR and role management
Week 6. Employee records and proper access control.

Tasks
Employee model and CRUD APIs
Employee list and form pages
Link a User account to an Employee
Admin screen to create users and assign roles
Audit every route and page against the permission matrix
Hide menu items per role in the UI, enforce on the server
Done when: The admin controls staff records and access, and each role sees only what it should.

Phase 5: Dashboard and reports
Week 7. Real-time insight for decisions.

Tasks
GET /dashboard/summary: stock value, today's sales, pending orders, low-stock count
Aggregation pipelines in reportService
Charts with Recharts: sales trend, top products, stock by category
Reports: sales, purchases, low stock, with date filters
CSV export
Automated report generation (scheduled with node-cron)
Done when: The dashboard updates with real data and reports can be filtered and exported.

Phase 6: Testing, deployment and final product
Week 8. Complete, polished, deployed SmartERP.

Tasks
Responsive layout, loading, empty and error states
Jest tests for services; Supertest tests for auth, roles and orders
Security pass: helmet, rate limiting, CORS, input sanitising
Seed script with realistic demo data
Deploy: server on Render, client on Vercel, database on Atlas
README, API docs, demo video, final report and presentation
Done when: The full product is live, tested and documented, ready for final review.

All six phases are in the tabs above, each with its tasks and a “Done when” check. Phase 6 is the finished product: tested, deployed and documented.

Each phase depends on the one before it, so don’t start Phase 3 until Phase 2’s stock logging works. Phase 3 is the hardest part of the project, so give it your best focus time

